// The high-frequency OSDP payloads.
//
// These are produced by the poll cycle, thousands of times a minute on a busy
// site, and they are the subset mirrored into a zero-copy schema. Everything
// else in this API is low-rate configuration and stays protobuf only.
//
// Two of them carry personal data -- a credential and a PIN -- which is why the
// mirror is worth the trouble: these are the messages that move, and they are
// also the messages that must not be casually copied into a log line.
//
